From 0fc2d593b7c68f996989bd16daef159882a7041e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Crittenden <rcritten@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2025 14:37:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Add initial ML-DSA support with NSS 3.112.0-4

NSS 3.112 has added support for Post-Quantum ML-DSA keys.
Allow them to be generated by certmonger.

The minimum key size is not fully implemented because key size
has a different meaning in this context. It is plumbed in, such that
one can set a numeric size, but it isn't used and is effectively
meaningless.

This includes what may be a temporary change to identify the key
type when reading a private key. NSS has an internal function
for this that may be exposed in the future. This works for now.
